# Campaign Health Assessment and Optimization System

## Executive Summary

We identified **22 campaigns** that experienced at least one month with cost > $1,000 and ROI < 0.8, signaling potential inefficiencies. Using a three‑dimensional health score model (Cost Efficiency 40%, Conversion Quality 35%, Competitiveness 25%), we evaluated all campaigns and flagged **3 high‑risk campaigns** that combine high cost, low ROI, and poor health scores. The analysis reveals significant performance variations across campaign types, bidding strategies, industries, geographies, and devices, as well as notable seasonal and year‑over‑year trends. Below we provide a detailed diagnosis for each risk segment, pinpoint root causes, and recommend actionable optimization plans.

## 1. Health Score Model & Risk Classification

### 1.1 Model Composition
- **Cost Efficiency (40%)**: Based on average ROI (return on investment) percentile rank.
- **Conversion Quality (35%)**: Average of conversion‑rate and quality‑score percentile ranks.
- **Competitiveness (25%)**: Average of CTR, impression‑share, and (inverted) average‑position percentile ranks.

Each metric is normalized to a 0–100 percentile across all campaigns; the weighted sum yields the final **Health Score** (0–100). Higher scores indicate better overall health.

### 1.2 Risk Levels
Campaigns are split into quartiles of Health Score:
- **Low** (top 25%)
- **Medium** (25–50%)
- **High** (50–75%)
- **Critical** (bottom 25%)

### 1.3 Overall Health Distribution
- **Mean Health Score**: 50.1
- **Standard Deviation**: 19.9
- **Range**: 14.9 (worst) – 82.2 (best)

## 2. High‑Cost, Low‑ROI Campaigns (Candidate List)

22 campaigns met the initial screening criterion (monthly cost > $1,000 and ROI < 0.8 at least once). These campaigns represent the primary focus for optimization.

## 3. High‑Risk Campaigns – Detailed Diagnosis

Three candidate campaigns also fall into the **High‑risk** category (Health Score in the bottom half). Their core problems are summarized below:

| Campaign ID | Campaign Name | Health Score | Risk Level | Lowest Dimension | Avg ROI | Avg Conv. Rate | Avg CTR | Avg Imp. Share | Avg Position |
|-------------|---------------|--------------|------------|------------------|---------|----------------|---------|----------------|--------------|
| 23 | Fashion – Search Campaign 23 | 60.3 | High | **Competitiveness** | 6.19 | 4.14% | 3.26% | 59.1% | 2.35 |
| 141 | Real Estate – Search Campaign 141 | 65.9 | High | **Competitiveness** | 6.58 | 4.49% | 3.36% | 54.5% | 2.32 |
| 157 | Healthcare – Search Campaign 157 | 50.5 | High | **Competitiveness** | 5.98 | 3.80% | 3.39% | 59.6% | 2.43 |

**Common Issue**: All three suffer from **low competitiveness**—relatively low impression share (54–60%) and average positions around 2.3–2.4, indicating they are losing auction share and visibility despite decent ROI and conversion rates.

## 4. Performance Differences Across Key Dimensions

### 4.1 Campaign Type
| Campaign Type | Avg ROI | Avg Conv. Rate | Avg CTR | Avg Imp. Share | Total Cost | Conversions per $ |
|---------------|---------|----------------|---------|----------------|------------|-------------------|
| **Shopping** | 13.01 | 5.31% | 4.27% | 61.8% | $3,758,047 | 0.033 |
| Performance Max | 7.32 | 4.06% | 3.52% | 63.1% | $2,239,362 | 0.019 |
| **Search** | 6.66 | 4.11% | 3.41% | 60.4% | $4,438,606 | 0.016 |
| **Video** | 4.44 | 1.00% | 0.80% | 47.8% | $4,556,255 | 0.013 |
| **Display** | 4.36 | 1.38% | 1.22% | 66.9% | $2,866,270 | 0.012 |

**Insight**: Shopping campaigns deliver the highest ROI and conversion efficiency, while Video and Display campaigns show lower ROI and conversion rates.

### 4.2 Bidding Strategy
| Bidding Strategy | Avg ROI | Avg Conv. Rate | Avg CTR | Avg Imp. Share | Conversions per $ |
|------------------|---------|----------------|---------|----------------|-------------------|
| Manual CPC | 8.54 | 4.52% | 3.62% | 59.6% | 0.020 |
| Enhanced CPC | 8.29 | 4.38% | 3.57% | 60.5% | 0.021 |
| Target ROAS | 7.97 | 4.20% | 3.44% | 59.8% | 0.021 |
| Maximize Conversions | 7.03 | 3.86% | 3.21% | 62.2% | 0.017 |
| Target CPA | 5.88 | 3.73% | 3.11% | 60.9% | 0.015 |

**Insight**: Manual and Enhanced CPC strategies yield the highest ROI; Target CPA lags behind.

### 4.3 Industry
| Industry | Avg ROI | Avg Conv. Rate | Avg CTR | Avg Imp. Share | Conversions per $ |
|----------|---------|----------------|---------|----------------|-------------------|
| Real Estate | 8.59 | 4.55% | 3.64% | 60.6% | 0.020 |
| E‑commerce | 9.01 | 4.87% | 3.89% | 61.1% | 0.026 |
| Finance | 7.48 | 3.82% | 3.13% | 61.0% | 0.018 |
| Education | 7.23 | 3.71% | 3.02% | 59.8% | 0.016 |
| Travel | 7.28 | 3.66% | 3.00% | 60.3% | 0.016 |
| Fashion | 7.13 | 3.78% | 3.10% | 60.1% | 0.018 |
| SaaS | 6.39 | 3.70% | 3.01% | 59.5% | 0.018 |
| Healthcare | 6.39 | 3.65% | 2.98% | 59.4% | 0.016 |

**Insight**: Real Estate and E‑commerce lead in ROI and conversion efficiency; Healthcare and SaaS are the lowest performers.

### 4.4 Geographic Distribution
| Geo Target | Avg ROI | Avg Conv. Rate | Avg CTR | Avg Imp. Share | Conversions per $ |
|------------|---------|----------------|---------|----------------|-------------------|
| United Kingdom | 8.46 | 4.41% | 3.60% | 61.3% | 0.020 |
| France | 7.76 | 4.08% | 3.33% | 60.8% | 0.019 |
| Australia | 7.75 | 4.06% | 3.31% | 60.7% | 0.019 |
| Japan | 7.44 | 3.90% | 3.18% | 60.5% | 0.018 |
| United States | 7.16 | 3.75% | 3.06% | 60.2% | 0.018 |
