# Analysis of Vocational School Graduates' Starting Salaries and Benefits

## 1. Introduction

This analysis uses job posting data for positions requiring "Vocational school or above" education. We aim to:

- Compute the distribution of starting salaries (lower bound of salary ranges).
- Identify the most common benefits offered.
- Determine which qualities (work experience, language skills, age, gender, company type, industry) significantly increase starting salaries.

The dataset includes 9,073 job postings for vocational school graduates. After parsing the salary range field, 7,936 postings had a valid starting salary.

## 2. Starting Salary Distribution

### Summary Statistics (yuan/month)
- **Mean**: 4,815.65
- **Median**: 4,500.00
- **Standard Deviation**: 1,918.10
- **Minimum**: 4
- **Maximum**: 30,000

### Distribution by Salary Bracket

| Salary Bracket | Count | Percentage |
|----------------|-------|------------|
| < 2,000        | 24    | 0.30%      |
| 2,000 - 2,999  | 226   | 2.85%      |
| 3,000 - 3,999  | 1,866 | 23.51%     |
| 4,000 - 4,999  | 2,438 | 30.72%     |
| 5,000 - 5,999  | 1,554 | 19.58%     |
| 6,000 - 6,999  | 912   | 11.49%     |
| 7,000 - 7,999  | 227   | 2.86%      |
| 8,000 - 8,999  | 382   | 4.81%      |
| 9,000 - 9,999  | 22    | 0.28%      |
| 10,000 - 14,999| 238   | 3.00%      |
| 15,000 - 19,999| 32    | 0.40%      |
| ≥ 20,000       | 15    | 0.19%      |

**Insight**: The majority of starting salaries (74.8%) fall between 3,000 and 6,000 yuan/month, with the modal bracket being 4,000‑4,999 yuan/month (30.7%). Only 3.9% of positions offer 10,000 yuan/month or more.

## 3. Benefits Distribution

We parsed the “Benefits” field, splitting by commas, semicolons, and Chinese punctuation. The total number of benefit mentions is 56,964 (multiple benefits per posting). The top 30 benefits are listed below; each percentage is relative to all benefit mentions.

| Rank | Benefit | Count | Percentage |
|------|---------|-------|------------|
| 1 | Five social insurances | 6,494 | 11.40% |
| 2 | paid annual leave | 4,630 | 8.13% |
| 3 | holiday benefits | 4,256 | 7.47% |
| 4 | performance bonus | 3,749 | 6.58% |
| 5 | housing provident fund | 2,492 | 4.37% |
| 6 | overtime pay | 2,175 | 3.82% |
| 7 | professional training | 2,143 | 3.76% |
| 8 | employee travel | 2,018 | 3.54% |
| 9 | meal allowance | 1,951 | 3.43% |
|10 | double pay at the end of the year | 1,869 | 3.28% |
|11 | commercial insurance | 1,840 | 3.23% |
|12 | full attendance bonus | 1,795 | 3.15% |
|13 | business trip allowance | 1,533 | 2.69% |
|14 | transportation allowance | 1,263 | 2.22% |
|15 | and full attendance bonus. | 1,237 | 2.17% |
|16 | communication allowance | 1,153 | 2.02% |
|17 | multiple salary adjustments per year | 1,044 | 1.83% |
|18 | and work uniform. | 1,040 | 1.83% |
|19 | high-temperature allowance | 1,035 | 1.82% |
|20 | meals provided | 881 | 1.55% |
|21 | housing allowance | 874 | 1.53% |
|22 | regular medical check-ups | 846 | 1.49% |
|23 | Five insurances | 590 | 1.04% |
|24 | and accommodation provided. | 583 | 1.02% |
|25 | year-end bonus | 580 | 1.02% |
|26 | free shuttle bus | 561 | 0.98% |
|27 | and meals provided. | 530 | 0.93% |
|28 | flexible working hours | 507 | 0.89% |
|29 | work uniform. | 475 | 0.83% |
|30 | high temperature allowance | 429 | 0.75% |

**Insight**: The most common benefits are **Five social insurances**, **paid annual leave**, and **holiday benefits**, appearing in over 10% of all benefit mentions. This suggests that compliance with labor law and basic welfare is widespread. **Performance bonuses** and **housing provident fund** also rank high, indicating that incentive pay and housing support are important.

## 4. Qualities That Increase Starting Salaries

We examine how different job requirements or employer characteristics correlate with higher starting salaries. For each factor, we compute the average starting salary of postings that specify that attribute (categories with at least 10 postings). The overall mean salary is 4,815.65 yuan/month.

### 4.1 Work Experience Requirement
Work experience has the strongest positive effect on starting salary. The more years required, the higher the average salary.

| Experience Requirement | Average Salary (yuan/month) | Count |
|------------------------|----------------------------|-------|
| Eight years or more    | 8,868.42                   | 19    |
| Ten years or more      | 7,642.86                   | 14    |
| Five years or more     | 6,911.94                   | 243   |
| Four years or more     | 6,588.24                   | 34    |
| Three years or more    | 5,784.12                   | 800   |
| Two years or more      | 5,021.51                   | 1,037 |
| No limit               | 4,545.33                   | 4,033 |
| More than one year     | 4,488.81                   | 1,582 |
| Fresh graduates        | 4,080.00                   | 155   |

**Key Takeaway**: Vocational graduates can expect a **2,000–4,000 yuan/month premium** if they have 5+ years of experience compared to fresh graduates.

### 4.2 Foreign Language Requirement
Jobs requiring foreign language skills, especially English, offer higher salaries.

| Language Requirement | Average Salary | Count |
|----------------------|----------------|-------|
| Proficiency in English required | 6,617.39 | 23 |
| Other levels require good performance. | 5,031.25 | 16 |
| Good Chinese proficiency required | 4,944.44 | 18 |
| Unspecified (no requirement) | 4,819.62 | 7,442 |
| English (general) | 4,715.38 | 195 |
| Good English proficiency required | 4,525.00 | 100 |

**Key Takeaway**: **English proficiency** (especially advanced) can boost salaries by about **1,800 yuan/month** relative to the overall mean.

### 4.3 Age Requirement
Certain age brackets are associated with higher salaries, likely because they correlate with experience.

| Age Requirement | Average Salary | Count |
|-----------------|----------------|-------|
| 30‑40 years old | 6,931.82 | 22 |
| 25‑38 years old | 6,545.45 | 22 |
| 30‑50 years old | 6,529.41 | 17 |
| 30‑45 years old | 6,258.06 | 62 |
| 26‑45 years old | 6,233.33 | 15 |

**Key Takeaway**: Jobs targeting **older workers (30‑45)** offer **1,500–2,100 yuan/month** above the mean, suggesting that maturity and experience are valued.

### 4.4 Gender Requirement
Most postings have no gender requirement (7,094), and those that do show a slight gender gap.

| Gender Requirement | Average Salary | Count |
|--------------------|----------------|-------|
| none               | 4,843.36 | 7,094 |
| female             | 4,617.07 | 785   |
| male               | 4,101.75 | 57    |

**Key Takeaway**: Positions without gender preference pay about **200‑700 yuan/month more** than those specifying a gender. This may reflect that gender-neutral roles are more professional and better compensated.

### 4.5 Company Type
Listed companies offer the highest average salary.

| Company Type | Average Salary | Count |
|--------------|----------------|-------|
| Listed companies | 5,248.88 | 178 |
