## Executive Summary
This analysis of the past year’s recruitment data supports the CEO’s mandate to reduce total recruitment costs by 15% while enhancing hiring quality, meeting diversity targets, and maintaining interviewer satisfaction above 4.0. The current recruitment cost is $27.87M, with an average cost per hire of $8,422. A 15% reduction would save $4.18M, bringing the target cost to $23.69M. Diversity benchmarks are already being met (female hire representation 42%, non‑white hire representation 32%). Interviewer satisfaction, measured by the average rating on scorecards, is currently 2.7, indicating a critical need for improvement. The proposed strategy reallocates sourcing channel investments, optimizes the interview process, and introduces targeted interviewer training to lift satisfaction above 4.0.

